  "description": "OQADET crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H154 N12 Nd7 O34 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+,8(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.706-4.776 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.36-149.56°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Et3NH[Nd7(L^{o-tBu})4(OH)6(NO3)4(EtOH)4]·(EtOH)8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
